++### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs: Agent Definitions and Onboarding
++
++- **slug:** The immutable machine identifier for the agent definition (e.g. `reality-checker`, `security-auditor`). Constrained to lowercase alphanumeric ASCII characters and hyphens. The slug forms the primary address for ticket comments, mention notifications, and REST endpoint routes (`/api/v1/admin/agent-definitions/:slug`).
++- **display_name:** The human-facing label rendered on board cards, ticket assignment selectors, peek drawers, and audit trails. Allows teams to provide intuitive persona titles (e.g. "Forensic QA Reality Checker" or "Architecture Auditor").
++- **harness_kind:** Specifies the runtime execution architecture. `in_app_sdk` executes in-process using configured cloud or local LLM providers. `cli_pipe` executes external command-line binaries (`agy`, `codex`) inside a zero-shell Linux namespace jail (`nsjail`), communicating strictly over standard input/output with 512 MB memory caps and zero network access. `remote_runner` dispatches tasks to distributed worker daemons connected over mutual TLS.
++- **provider_kind and model_id:** Applicable to `in_app_sdk` harnesses. Specifies the active provider backend (`gemini`, `openai`, `ollama`) and specific model (e.g. `gemini-2.5-flash`, `gpt-4o`, `llama3.2:latest`) utilized for the agent persona's completion and tool-calling cycles.
++- **cli_binary_allowlist_id and cli_args:** Governs `cli_pipe` execution. Restricts binary invocations to pre-vetted host binaries (`agy`, `codex`). Arguments are submitted as an array of safe flags (default `["-p"]`) executed directly via `execve`, eliminating shell injection hazards (`/bin/sh` is never spawned).
++- **remote_runner_pool_slug:** Designates the distributed worker pool (such as `default` or `gpu-compute`) responsible for accepting tasks when `harness_kind = remote_runner`.
++- **repo_access_mode:** Enforces Git repository access boundaries during task execution. In `none` mode, the agent operates solely on ticket prose. In `ro_vfs_mount` mode, the target repository is mounted strictly read-only (`CLONE_NEWNS`), allowing static code analysis while preventing unauthorized workspace writes. In `bare_git_tools` mode, read-only bare Git inspection tools are provisioned in an isolated tmpfs directory.
++- **mcp_allowed_tools:** An array of tool names defining the explicit Model Context Protocol allowlist for the agent. Tools outside this list (`search_tickets`, `read_ticket`, `search_knowledge`, `read_doc`) are hidden from the agent's schema, enforcing strict privilege separation (submitting unlisted tools fails with HTTP 422 `HARNESS_FIELDS_INVALID`).
++- **system_instructions_md:** The core persona prompt formatted in canonical UTF-8 Markdown. Directs agent analysis, defines verification standards, and specifies output formats. Server-side sanitization strips lone surrogates and harmful prompt injection vectors before database storage.
++- **timeout_ms:** Maximum allowable execution time for agent invocations, configurable from 1,000 ms to 300,000 ms (default 60,000 ms, adhering to the 300-second reasoning ceiling from KAN-430). Tasks that exceed this threshold are terminated immediately, preserving thread pools and avoiding stuck workflows.
++- **project_id and rls_isolation:** Binds the agent definition to a specific project UUID or leaves it at workspace scope. PostgreSQL `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` strictly isolates project agents: administrators and members of other projects cannot view, mutate, or validate cross-project agents (returning HTTP 404 Not Found).
++- **agent_validation_modal:** Invoked via `POST /api/v1/admin/agent-definitions/:id:validate` or `POST /api/v1/agent-definitions/:id:validate`. Executes a live non-destructive test invocation returning a 4-section forensic verification report: 1. `=== 1. RENDERED CONTEXT ===`, 2. `=== 2. TOOL TRACE ===`, 3. `=== 3. LATENCY & TOKENS ===`, and 4. `=== 4. SCHEMA & POLICY STATUS ===`.
++- **llms_txt_and_onboarding_card:** Machine-readable agent capabilities and skill manifests served at `/llms.txt`. The onboarding card surfaces the canonical onboarding prompt that guides external agents (Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, Gemini CLI) through an interactive setup interview, persisting user preferences (`execution_mode`, `model_strategy`, `qa_rigor`, `custom_notes`) to `agent_onboarding_prefs` in `/api/v1/users/me/preferences` strictly within the local project folder without polluting global system paths.
